// SNDINFO - the sound catalogue. Each line maps a LOGICAL name (what the
// code asks for, e.g. A_StartSound("sd/weapon/ppsh/fire")) to a LUMP (the
// actual audio data). ZDoom wiki: https://zdoom.org/wiki/SNDINFO
//
// F4 status: every entry below points at a Freedoom (IWAD) lump as a
// PLACEHOLDER. Nothing is redistributed - the engine resolves the name
// against the loaded IWAD. When sound-designer delivers the real files into
// src/sounds/ (lump name = file name without extension), only the right-hand
// column changes; no ZScript is touched. The requested lump names are in the
// comment at the end of each line.

// --- Slot 1: sapper's shovel ---------------------------------------------
// The SWING (blade cutting the air) is DELIBERATELY SILENT in F4. Freedoom
// has no neutral whoosh: the only swing-through-air lump is DSSKESWG, the
// revenant's melee wind-up, and borrowing it would teach the player that a
// monster is about to punch them every time they raise the shovel. Doom's
// own Fist has no swing sound either - the feedback is the impact. The
// placeholder DSSAWUP (chainsaw start-up) was rejected by the CEO on
// 2026-10-13 and is not replaced: a wrong sound is worse than none.
// When sound-designer delivers SDSHSWG, add back BOTH lines:
//     sd/weapon/shovel/swing  SDSHSWG
//   and in src/zscript/weapons/shovel.zs, Fire state, first frame:
//     PUNG B 5 A_StartSound("sd/weapon/shovel/swing", CHAN_WEAPON);
// (tests/test_arsenal.py enforces that the two stay in step: a logical name
// defined here with nothing playing it fails, and vice versa.)
sd/weapon/shovel/hit       DSPUNCH     // -> SDSHHIT  steel into a body

// --- Slot 2: TT-33 Tokarev -----------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/tokarev/fire     DSPISTOL    // -> SDTTFIR  dry, high-velocity crack

// --- Slot 3: IZh-58 double barrel ----------------------------------------
sd/weapon/izh/fire         DSSHOTGN    // -> SDIZFIR  one barrel, deep boom
sd/weapon/izh/reload       DSSGCOCK    // -> SDIZRLD  break open, two shells, snap shut

// --- Slot 4: PPSh-41 ------------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/ppsh/fire        DSPISTOL    // -> SDPPFIR  fast, tinny, drum rattle

// --- Slot 5: RPG-7 --------------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/rpg7/fire        DSRLAUNC    // -> SDRPFIR  launch whoosh plus motor
sd/weapon/rpg7/explode     DSBAREXP    // -> SDRPEXP  shaped-charge crack

// --- Slot 6: ROKS-3 flamethrower -----------------------------------------
sd/weapon/roks3/fire       DSFLAME     // -> SDRKFIR  short pressurised burst

// --- Slot 7: hand Katyusha ------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/katyusha/charge  DSBFG       // -> SDHKCHG  rails rising, 20 tics
sd/weapon/katyusha/fire    DSRLAUNC    // -> SDHKFIR  six rockets off the rails
sd/weapon/katyusha/burst   DSBAREXP    // -> SDHKEXP  one rocket detonating

// === Bestiary (F5) =========================================================
// Logical names sd/mon/<actor>/<event>; the final lump is the name in the
// comment, the one docs/sound/ENEMY-SOUNDS.md has a card for (sound-designer
// owns that column). 47 lumps: docs/engine/BESTIARY.md 12. Every
// placeholder below is a Freedoom (IWAD) lump, read from the IWAD at run
// time and never redistributed; tests/test_bestiary.py checks each exists.
// Two placeholders are knowingly imperfect: the rifleman fires DSPISTOL,
// which the TT-33 also uses (the final SDRRIATK must not), and the
// General's order is DSVILSIT, a creature's sight, until SDGENSUM exists.

// --- Reich rifleman (SD_ReichRifleman) -------------------------------------
sd/mon/reichrifleman/active   DSPOSACT    // -> SDRRIACT  muttered order
sd/mon/reichrifleman/sight    DSPOSIT1    // -> SDRRISIT  short bark
sd/mon/reichrifleman/attack   DSPISTOL    // -> SDRRIATK  dry bolt-action crack
sd/mon/reichrifleman/pain     DSPOPAIN    // -> SDRRIPAI
sd/mon/reichrifleman/death    DSPODTH1    // -> SDRRIDTH
sd/mon/reichrifleman/xdeath   DSSLOP      // -> SDRRIXDT  gib

// --- Liberty Legion trooper (SD_LegionTrooper) -----------------------------
sd/mon/legiontrooper/active   DSPOSACT    // -> SDLTRACT  radio chatter
sd/mon/legiontrooper/sight    DSPOSIT2    // -> SDLTRSIT
sd/mon/legiontrooper/attack   DSDSHTGN    // -> SDLTRATK  not DSSHOTGN: that is the IZh's
sd/mon/legiontrooper/pain     DSPOPAIN    // -> SDLTRPAI
sd/mon/legiontrooper/death    DSPODTH2    // -> SDLTRDTH
sd/mon/legiontrooper/xdeath   DSSLOP      // -> SDLTRXDT

// --- Hybrid Stormtrooper (SD_Stormtrooper, SD_StormBolt) -------------------
sd/mon/stormtrooper/active    DSBGACT     // -> SDSTOACT
sd/mon/stormtrooper/sight     DSBGSIT1    // -> SDSTOSIT
sd/mon/stormtrooper/melee     DSCLAW      // -> SDSTOMEL
sd/mon/stormtrooper/missile   DSFIRSHT    // -> SDSTOMIS  bolt launch (the bolt's SeeSound)
sd/mon/stormtrooper/explode   DSFIRXPL    // -> SDSTOEXP  bolt impact (its DeathSound)
sd/mon/stormtrooper/pain      DSDMPAIN    // -> SDSTOPAI
sd/mon/stormtrooper/death     DSBGDTH1    // -> SDSTODTH
sd/mon/stormtrooper/xdeath    DSSLOP      // -> SDSTOXDT

